// The Vault's own Git metadata: syncing a live repository across devices
// corrupts the index. Anchored to the root on purpose — an unanchored `.git`
// would also strip the history of every project repository kept under assets/.
/.git

// OS junk. The (?d) prefix lets Syncthing delete these when it removes a
// directory that a remote device deleted — without it, leftover junk keeps the
// directory non-empty and the folder stays permanently out of sync.
(?d).DS_Store
(?d)._*
(?d).Spotlight-V100
(?d).Trashes
(?d).fseventsd
(?d).TemporaryItems
(?d).apdisk
(?d)Thumbs.db
(?d)desktop.ini
(?d)$RECYCLE.BIN

// Obsidian machine-local state (do not sync window/pane layout across devices)
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.trash

// Editor / temp / lock files
(?d)*.tmp
(?d)~$*
(?d).~lock.*
(?d)*.swp
(?d)*.swo

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Machine-local build output and dependency trees.
//
// Two replicas that build the same artefact rewrite it in full and
// independently, which Syncthing can only read as a concurrent edit — a
// guaranteed conflict, not a race that better timing would win. Everything
// below is derived: deleting it costs a rebuild, never a source file.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Lean/Lake build artifacts (multi-GB, machine-local; e.g. assets/1-projects/PQCPlus/Formalization)
(?d)**/.lake

// Python virtual environments. The interpreter and the compiled wheels inside
// are platform-specific, so a venv replicated from macOS to Linux is not merely
// redundant but broken on arrival.
(?d)**/.venv

// Node dependency trees. Reinstallable from the lockfile, and large enough by
// file count to dominate the folder index on their own.
(?d)**/node_modules

// Python bytecode and tool caches. The .pyc magic number is tied to the
// interpreter version, so these are wrong rather than merely stale on a replica
// running a different Python.
(?d)**/__pycache__
(?d)*.pyc
(?d)**/.pytest_cache
(?d)**/.mypy_cache
(?d)**/.ruff_cache
(?d)**/.ipynb_checkpoints
(?d)**/.tox
(?d)**/*.egg-info

// Visual Studio / MSBuild leftovers, from the archived C++ coursework. Records
// of one machine's build environment: absolute include paths, incremental-build
// state, per-user window layout.
(?d)**/.vs
(?d)**/*.tlog
(?d)*.vcxproj.user
(?d)*.suo

// General opt-out: anything named stignore-* stays on the machine that made it.
// Point build tools here (latexmk `$out_dir`, and so on) whenever their output
// is derived, rewritten wholesale on every run, and therefore guaranteed to
// collide between two replicas. The name states its own purpose, so an
// unfamiliar directory needs no lookup to be understood.
(?d)**/stignore-*

// LaTeX intermediates, regenerated in full by every compile. Named after the
// document, so two machines building the same paper collide on all of them at
// once.
//
// Four extensions are deliberately absent. .bbl is what an arXiv submission
// ships and the output .pdf is often the artefact being shared, so neither is
// disposable. .log and .out name a LaTeX intermediate here but a job's stdout
// or a compiled binary elsewhere; no pattern distinguishes the two, and an
// exemption list that has to enumerate every directory holding real results is
// a rule that fails silently the first time one is forgotten. Both stay in the
// sync set, and a document built on two machines at once is kept out of
// conflict the same way everything else is: by pointing $out_dir at
// stignore-*.
(?d)*.aux
(?d)*.bcf
(?d)*.blg
(?d)*.brf
(?d)*.fdb_latexmk
(?d)*.fls
(?d)*.idx
(?d)*.ilg
(?d)*.ind
(?d)*.lof
(?d)*.lot
(?d)*.nav
(?d)*.run.xml
(?d)*.snm
(?d)*.synctex.gz
(?d)*.toc
(?d)*.vrb
(?d)*.xdv

// Zotero's regenerable state, beside the library in assets/2-areas/Zotero. The
// full-text cache is re-extracted per machine; the SQLite journal and WAL are
// transaction state, and a mid-write snapshot of them is precisely what turns a
// replicated database into a corrupt one.
(?d)**/.zotero-ft-cache
(?d)**/.zotero-ft-info
(?d)zotero.sqlite-journal
(?d)zotero.sqlite-wal
(?d)zotero.sqlite-shm
